WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.490
Welcome to Master 02 for EXL Salesforce COE Resource 360.

2
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:18.410
This live Salesforce walkthrough follows one project from portfolio selection through its account and commercial lineage, resource roster, budget economics, actual effort, dynamic work plan, accountable risks and effective-dated allocation history.

3
00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:26.493
Filters, selections, drill-downs and action outcomes are all performed on the authenticated product using the rich fictional dataset.

4
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.044
ENG-01 starts with the scoped engagement portfolio.

5
00:00:32.044 --> 00:00:39.872
We filter to active delivery, search for Global Retail, select Global Retail Cloud and open its Project 360.

6
00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:45.960
The selected card carries account, portfolio, industry, solution tower, completion, health and risk context.

7
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:52.048
Salesforce sharing and the active persona determine the rows returned by this live selector.

8
00:00:53.248 --> 00:00:58.533
ENG-02 reconciles account, portfolio, sub-portfolio and delivery ownership around the selected project.

9
00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:04.698
Its commercial chain preserves the original SOW, amendment and change order as separate versions.

10
00:01:04.698 --> 00:01:15.267
We select the amendment, inspect its value, validity and accepted line, then drill into the related work plan before continuing to the project roster.

11
00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:20.797
ENG-03 shows the effective project roster, not a contact list.

12
00:01:20.797 --> 00:01:31.190
We filter to Billing, search for Riya Sen, select an allocation and inspect daily hours, capacity state, effective dates, over-allocation control and skill evidence.

13
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:38.985
Opening the practitioner Resource 360 proves the roster supports real record drill-down before we return to project economics.

14
00:01:40.185 --> 00:01:43.684
ENG-04 connects signed commercial authority to project economics.

15
00:01:43.684 --> 00:01:48.933
We filter approved budgets, select the current version and review approval evidence.

16
00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:56.368
Revenue, planned cost, gross margin, forecast margin, EAC, ETC and the costed role roster remain visible together.

17
00:01:56.368 --> 00:02:02.929
The outcome exposes policy and approval context instead of treating the status badge as proof.

18
00:02:04.129 --> 00:02:07.401
ENG-05 reconciles actual effort with the selected project.

19
00:02:07.401 --> 00:02:13.127
We filter to Submitted, select a weekly timesheet and run the eight-hour daily-cap validation.

20
00:02:13.127 --> 00:02:17.217
The screen shows workflow state, exception evidence and daily entries.

21
00:02:17.217 --> 00:02:27.033
Planned over-allocation can be controlled elsewhere, while actual time remains capped at eight hours per day unless a separately governed overtime policy is enabled.

22
00:02:28.233 --> 00:02:31.155
ENG-06 is the project manager work plan.

23
00:02:31.155 --> 00:02:36.581
We filter to Build, select a WBS item and isolate the critical path.

24
00:02:36.581 --> 00:02:41.590
The detail panel exposes owner, schedule, progress, acceptance, effort and dependency evidence.

25
00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:51.190
The final action opens the related risk register, connecting schedule exceptions to accountable mitigation rather than leaving the Gantt as a passive picture.

26
00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.633
ENG-07 makes delivery risk actionable.

27
00:02:54.633 --> 00:03:02.706
We filter for high-severity risks in mitigation, select the consent and identity-resolution item and acknowledge the accountable action.

28
00:03:02.706 --> 00:03:07.191
Owner, due date, mitigation and visible acknowledgement outcome remain together.

29
00:03:07.191 --> 00:03:13.919
This gives project, portfolio and operations roles the same attributable evidence from trigger through response.

30
00:03:15.119 --> 00:03:19.272
ENG-08 closes the project journey with effective-dated allocation lineage.

31
00:03:19.272 --> 00:03:22.503
We select another practitioner and compare versions.

32
00:03:22.503 --> 00:03:30.810
The screen preserves role, hours, effective window, acceptance, billing classification, publication evidence and capacity state for each line.

33
00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:38.655
Prior versions remain immutable, while only the current accepted version drives capacity, utilization and authorized time entry.
